Misho put the frontend first and answered both questions: the chain in
stages, the member card as the frontend listed it. Both routes are keyed
by the sealed id the contacts list already carries.

- GET /members/:id: name, role, company, city, areas, open_to (the
  member's own saved offers). Work hides under hideUserWorkInfo, areas and
  offers under hideUserTags. 404 for a foreign id or a non-member.
- GET /paths/:id: up to 3 maps, each the owner, up to three members in
  the middle, the target (4 steps). Only paths whose every middle person is
  a member; blocks checked at every step in both directions; fewest steps,
  then most warm steps. Links carry name, role, state (next /
  not_contacted) and the member card id. Nothing is sent.

findWarmPath's name lookup is exported and shared. §127 recorded in
ADMIN_WRITE_OPERATIONS; the contract is in FOR_FRONTEND.

